# Typecheck before push

`next dev` does not run the full compiler. Vercel’s first `next build` is often the first time the whole app is typechecked, which is why main deploys fail on missing names and unused vars.

Before `git push` (and before treating a TypeScript/React change as done):

```bash
npm run typecheck
```

Fix every error. Do not push a red `tsc` and wait for Vercel to catch it.
